  "limitations": [
    "Staged v0.13.0 binds OMP 18.12.6, rebased RTX 5090 source 04b603aa on upstream 64d10fbf, published model 81f924d4 and configuration c73eb8fb. Root authority/profiles stay on v0.12.2 until lane pin. Council disposition and fresh client/public-route acceptance are not granted by runtime eligibility.",
    "The client is the unmodified upstream OMP binary and has no appliance commands. Documented installation/lifecycle routes remain authoritative; no client reads the compatibility authority.",
    "Checkpoint schema 3 uses isolated /checkpoints-v013. Do not mount, scan, import or migrate v0.12.x roots; keep old roots untouched for rollback and replay prior sessions from authoritative OMP transcripts.",
    "Checkpointing remains best effort under live traffic. A crash or an expired graceful wait can lose unpublished acceleration state; zero queueing, loss-free shutdown and universal warm reuse are not promised.",
    "JSON-schema structured output is supported on the rebased RTX 5090 by grammar/product smoke; carried native packages still reject it with HTTP 400 and retain 64-character tool names. The rebased container accepts 128-character names. Stock-client/public-route acceptance is a separate gate.",
    "The RTX 5090 profile has 146368 automatic BF16 KV tokens, 131072 logical context, DFlash2 K=7, two active requests and two extra device-state slots. Two requests run together only while their prompts/output reservations fit; pending timeout is 180 seconds. No constant-batch-two throughput or universal prefill/decode fairness is claimed.",
    "Carried native v0.6.11 RTX 4090 and v0.6.3 RTX 3090 packages/model eec39564 remain unchanged, GPU-UUID-bound and sequential on port 18082; fresh OMP 18.12.6 public-install/client acceptance is required. Rebased 24 GB natives need the K5 admission-headroom amendment and independent packaging/qualification for v0.13.1.",
    "RTX 4090 has no supported rollback target on its two-GPU lineage. RTX 3090 retains its actual qualified predecessor. Runtime upgrade qualification does not activate production.",
    "Powered quality/leak, full-model output/acceptance parity, historical actual OMP parallel dispatch, long-client/fanout/warm-arrival latency, and full G2 after canonical serialization are not re-measured for v0.13.0; scoped current tests are not substitutes.",
    "Multi-GPU inference, simultaneous native serving, multi-tenant operation, priority guarantees and silent cloud fallback are unsupported. macOS remains preview; Linux live evidence is WSL2-scoped. Measured throughput/latency belongs only to its recorded workload, binary, artifact and profile."
  ],
